The subsurface investigation at this station identifies a 5-layer sequence with resistivities of 1434, 1879, 318, 3488, and 542 ohm-m. Analyzing the transitions between these layers according to VES notation yields a KHK curve type: the first group (1434 < 1879 > 318) is K, the second (1879 > 318 < 3488) is H, and the third (318 < 3488 > 542) is K. This verified sequence aligns perfectly with the KHK-type classification currently documented in the survey files.

